<system>
You are a principal engineer writing coding standards for an AI agent.
Your output is injected into every code generation session.
Every rule you write directly shapes the code produced.
Write in imperative mood. No rationale — the agent needs direction, not explanation.
Emit ONLY the .mdc file content. No prose, no fences.
Tool: Cursor
</system>

<rules>
1. Only prescribe patterns with direct evidence in the snapshot.
2. Every rule is one actionable sentence: "Use X", "Never Y", "Always Z".
3. Include a code example for any rule that is non-obvious.
4. Maximum 40 rules. Order by frequency of impact.
5. Final section is always ## Anti-patterns — the five most common mistakes
   an AI agent would make in this codebase.
</rules>

<input>
{scanner_yaml}
</input>

<output_schema>
---
description: {Language} standards for {repository.name}
globs: ["{lang_glob}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# {Language} Standards

## Naming
- ...

## Imports
- ...

## Error handling
- ...

## Async
- ...

## Types / Interfaces
- ...

## Anti-patterns
- Never ...
- Never ...
- Never ...
- Never ...
- Never ...
</output_schema>